== Description == <!--T:2-->

<!--T:3-->
[[File:Std_LinkImport.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkImport|Std LinkImport]] imports the {{PropertyData|Linked Object}} from a Link into the current document, and then changes the attachment to this object.

<!--T:4-->
This operation is helpful when working with [[Assembly|assemblies]] in order to organize re-usable models that may be located in other documents.

<!--T:5-->
Use [[File:Std_LinkImportAll.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkImportAll|Std LinkImportAll]] to import all linked objects.

== Usage == <!--T:6-->

<!--T:7-->
# Make sure you have a "source" document with an original object, say, a [[File:Std_Part.svg|16px]] [[Std_Part|Std Part]], and a second "target" document with a Link to that object.
# Open the target document and select the Link to the object; its {{PropertyData|Linked Object}} property should show something like {{Value|source#Part}}.
# There are several ways to invoke the command:
#* Press the {{Button|[[File:Std_LinkImport.svg|16px]] [[Std_LinkImport|Import Links]]}} button.
#* Select the {{MenuCommand|Edit → Create → Link Actions → [[Image:Std_LinkImport.svg|16px]] Import Links}} option from the menu. {{Version|26.3}}

<!--T:8-->
A copy of the original [[File:Std_Part.svg|16px]] [[Std_Part|Std Part]] must now be inside the current "target" document. The {{PropertyData|Linked Object}} property of the Link must now show {{Value|Part}}, indicating that the Link no longer points to {{Value|Part}} in "source", but to {{Value|Part}} in the current document ("target").

